## description

the blog app serves as an open workspace and publishing journal managed by Pendoncete within the pendoncete.org ecosystem. conceived as an open notebook of essays, guides, and technical notes, the blog bridges diverse subjects that refuse to fit into neat boxes—spanning carnal and sensual dimensions, bodily pleasure, and intimate memory alongside classical history, medieval chronicles, polytonic languages, and complex web architecture.

posts are freely available for any visitor to read, while active participation such as leaving comments and joining discussions requires registration within the ecosystem.

## sections and access

- **homepage (`/`)**: central landing view highlighting recent articles, technical walkthroughs, and project updates.
- **info (`/info`)**: editorial overview detailing the author's philosophy, the synthesis of intellectual and corporeal topics, and platform access rules.
- **posts**: complete collection of articles, essays, and technical notes, filterable by date, language, or status.
- **categories**: structured archives organizing topics by subject and perspective, mapping technical work, linguistics, history, and culture into objective descriptions and personal notes.
- **comments / discussions (registration required)**: interactive feedback spaces allowing registered users and subscribers to engage with published content.

